WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.104
(bright upbeat music)

00:00:03.104 --> 00:00:06.090
- [Malcolm] Here in this part of Chicago

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:07.810
a lot of folks list this neighborhood

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:09.134
as a food desert.

00:00:09.134 --> 00:00:12.010
A lot of places that
got abandoned buildings

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:14.510
but not a place that do
a lot of healthy food

00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:15.510
in the neighborhood.

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:20.000
I want to take the
opportunity to go around,

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.440
show people how to farm,

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:23.773
show 'em that this type
of work is healing.

00:00:26.279 --> 00:00:30.250
- [Narrator] This Great
Big Story was made possible

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:32.420
by Horizon Organic.

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:37.420
(bright upbeat music)

00:00:44.441 --> 00:00:48.370
- My name is Malcolm Evans.
I am the farm manager here

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:49.770
at Urban Growers Collective.

00:00:50.839 --> 00:00:54.810
The farm we own now is
the South Chicago farm

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:56.865
and this our main farm here.

00:00:56.865 --> 00:01:00.143
We grow all different type a vegetables:

00:01:00.143 --> 00:01:04.700
spinach, spring onions, arugula,

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:06.583
lettuce mix, collard greens,

00:01:06.583 --> 00:01:08.623
different type of varieties of radishes.

00:01:09.565 --> 00:01:11.700
After we harvest it we put it on the bus

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:12.533
for Fresh Move.

00:01:14.769 --> 00:01:17.980
- Fresh Move's mobile market

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:19.810
is literally a market that moves.

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:21.900
It's a Chicago Transit authority bus

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:24.630
that got transformed into a place

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:26.500
where people can come on board.

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:28.380
Instead of going to the destination,

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:30.494
can purchase healthy food.

00:01:30.494 --> 00:01:34.890
Our focus for Fresh
Moves geographically is

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:37.371
the South Side and the
West Side of Chicago.

00:01:37.371 --> 00:01:39.310
These neighborhoods have historically

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:41.172
not had healthy food access.

00:01:41.172 --> 00:01:42.590
- This one, give it about one more day,

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:44.343
it's ready to go, like
put it on your windowsill.

00:01:44.343 --> 00:01:48.014
- We harvest and sell probably
two tons of food every week.

00:01:48.014 --> 00:01:50.545
We're able to bring the freshest,

00:01:50.545 --> 00:01:53.387
highest quality affordable produce.

00:01:53.387 --> 00:01:56.630
We have really consistent folks

00:01:56.630 --> 00:01:59.044
who come and shop and people love it.

00:01:59.044 --> 00:02:02.180
They joke when their
favorite thing is not there.

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:03.930
And, you know, come back and expect

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:04.890
to see it next week;

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:08.320
and it's a pretty joyful
exchange between everybody

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:11.260
and definitely like keeps
us motivated to know

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:13.030
that the work that we're doing makes such

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:14.325
a big difference.

00:02:14.325 --> 00:02:16.608
- [Malcolm] I definitely see more folks

00:02:16.608 --> 00:02:17.960
when I'm doing a Fresh Move

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:21.100
programs coming on the bus
learning about vegetables

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:23.863
and me talking about how
healthy this piece is for them.

00:02:24.842 --> 00:02:28.670
Coming here, seeing this stuff grow

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:29.920
that I put in the ground,

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:32.270
I feel like when I do the work that I do,

00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:33.883
I accomplish something.

00:02:33.883 --> 00:02:35.930
It make me feel like, yeah,

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:37.700
these people is paying attention.

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:39.926
They see that this food is life.

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:43.093
(bright upbeat music)

